+# Request 14: reader-image and archive-PDF page-position test
+
+**TEL01.** The [previously acquired 28-page archive PDF](../telephone-doj-request14-member-2026-11-15/README.md), SHA-256 `957eecd527e1f1ee56867704b630c81edb766e76b8519b95abb5e660ac335f20`, was compared to the 28 previously preserved reader JPEGs, each checked against the [published image manifest](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/ad7be60185f5d3a49f0e0b7564f4da3610afaf92/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-carrier-enclosures-2026-10-27/SOURCE-IMAGES.json). The PDF was acquired 2026-11-15 and the reader images 2026-10-27.
+
+**Result.** Each of the 28 reader pages had its highest image-pattern correlation with the PDF page at the same position. Same-position correlations ranged from **0.985 to 0.990**; the highest comparison against a different-position page was **0.665**. The smallest same-page advantage over the best different-page comparison was **0.323**. SOURCE-PINS.json retains all 28 scores. This supports a visual page-position correspondence between these particular copies, rather than a claim that they are byte-identical, complete, independently sourced or authenticated as the original delivery.
+
+**Method.** The PDF was rendered at 100 dpi; each rendering and JPEG was converted to grayscale, resized to 192 × 192 pixels and standardized by its mean and standard deviation. The script computes every reader-to-PDF pixel-vector correlation and compares same-position scores with all other positions as controls. This coarse, whole-page test can miss different text, redactions, fine digits or inserted details; it is not a transcription or a forensic image-equivalence test. The sources contain sensitive fields: the published derivative includes only metrics, source hashes and code. [Reproduction script](compare.py) requires the PDF, manifest and reader images, plus Pillow, NumPy and `pdftoppm`; it writes renderings to a user-specified new directory.
+
+**Unresolved.** The cover describes 50 enclosed pages, the archive PDF has 28 pages including that cover, and the separate visible-label census records 600–608 followed by 632–645. Those observations remain intact; the comparison does not determine the original delivery's contents, why these copies have their current scope, or whether any other version exists. The prior **7555 / 7565** readings remain unresolved, and this downsampled test cannot distinguish them. Obtain the delivery manifest, full production, native carrier data, field definitions and an independent digit reading. No conclusion about missing-page cause, wrongdoing, call identity or duration follows.
